* Missing stimulus guidance: generate distinct-target concurrency, same-target contention, long target stalls, decode misses, and arbitration handover.
* Missing coverage: topology type, number of active initiators, same/different target, arbitration result, stall duration, response type, and fairness outcome.
* The exercise only asks which topology has the highest concurrency. It does not test route contention, ordering, or response ownership.

