### [03_timing_diagrams — Timing Diagrams]

Status: Major Revisions

Accuracy Audit:

* The statement that a receiver sees a request on one edge, computes a response, and the sender sees it only on the following edge describes one possible registered implementation—not a universal protocol rule.
* AHB response information can be produced during the data phase and sampled on its completion edge. AXI channel latency depends on implementation and inserted register stages.
* Pipelining does not automatically mean “multiple in-flight transactions.” AHB overlaps the address phase of one transfer with the data phase of the previous transfer, but does not provide AXI-style outstanding transaction IDs.
